<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Document xmlns:p="property" xmlns:r="reflection" Id="FDTX7Ie2jAGYlj7tpZaiyi" LanguageVersion="2025.7.4" Version="0.128">
  <NugetDependency Id="SIMDywDLwNbQ5UdOPHQxYD" Location="VL.CoreLib" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="Sm17wEPgUJCVB75op3gzPF" Location="VL.Skia" Version="2025.7.4" />
  <NugetDependency Id="CCoTJSCcdlnfZwmjUnPFVB" Location="VL.Mapsui" Version="0.0.0" />
  <!--
    NetTopologySuite is declared HERE, by this document, and that is not the same as VL.Mapsui
    declaring it. VL.Mapsui's own declaration is what lets its node signatures name NTS types; a
    patch that wants to use NTS nodes itself needs its own dependency on it. Measured: without this
    line the node below is "Not found"; with it, it resolves.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="KkbVvAgR3UtmSGnGV4pAoR" Location="NetTopologySuite" Version="2.6.0" />
  <!--
    VL.NetTopologySuite is the package that MAKES geometry; this one draws it. VL.Mapsui's nuspec
    depends on it so that opening this patch does not greet you with red nodes - vvvv does not
    fetch a missing document dependency by itself, it shows it red and offers to install on
    rightclick.
  -->
  <NugetDependency Id="QVnZMbPyNO4lv6YFocyiqT" Location="VL.NetTopologySuite" Version="0.0.1-alpha" />
  <Patch Id="FJzZkKqVfW12i9kQk6L0hz">
    <Canvas Id="N0E8bKG5vqG1aLaGsfcogC" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <!--

    ************************ Application ************************

-->
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pt4eKK7Ag0dikcitT4Vmar">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="T1yChjTcVpcQLJ4rxMEL44">
        <Canvas Id="VxYLn5bECvkjhyGerEE3sc" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="VaZNqihOnpwz6dORWEdpu0" Bounds="60,30,620,300" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Several layers on one map, and the two things that decide what you see: ORDER and RANGE.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;LAYER ORDER IS SPREAD ORDER. Three layers go into one Cons and out to the Map: a basemap, an area, and a line. The tile layer goes into Input, so everything else lands on top of it, and the line goes in after the area so it draws over it. Swap the two links and watch which one wins.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THERE IS NO Z-INDEX, AT EITHER LEVEL. Mapsui's ILayer carries thirteen properties and not one of them is ordering; the word ZIndex does not appear in VL.Skia at all. Position IS the order - the index in Map.Layers here, the pin or spread order in Skia's Group outside. Mapsui's layer GROUPS are a version 5 feature; 4.1.9 has Add, Insert at an index, and Move, and nothing else.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;SO ORDER THE SPREAD IN BANDS, bottom to top: raster, then polygons, then lines, then points, then labels. That is the order every cartography text gives and every GIS ships. With many layers, build each band separately and concatenate them - that is Mapsui 5's layer groups done by hand, and it makes the order something you can read rather than something that happened.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ORDER DOES NOT REDUCE ANYTHING. Twenty layers all draw, whatever the order. VISIBLERANGE is what reduces: it gives a layer the zoom levels it belongs to, and outside them Mapsui skips it. Measured: 91204 pixels inside the range, 0 outside - a hard cut, not a fade. Zoom out past 10 here and the line leaves; zoom back in and it returns, while the area and the basemap are untouched.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Its two pins run OPPOSITE to the numbers underneath. Mapsui stores this as MinVisible and MaxVisible in RESOLUTION - map units per pixel - where a higher zoom is a SMALLER number, so From Zoom sets MaxVisible. The node hides that. Range Status says what it understood, and a backwards range is refused rather than obeyed, because obeying it hides the layer at every zoom and that looks exactly like data that failed to load.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;ONE TRAP THAT ORDER CANNOT FIX: labels do not float to the top. A label belongs to a feature's style INSIDE a layer, so it is drawn when that layer is drawn - and a layer above covers it. Measured: a labelled point put down 28 pixels of label ink alone, and 0 with a polygon layer above it. Cartography says labels go last; Mapsui says layers go in order. To have both, put the labels in their OWN layer, last in the spread: the same features into another FeatureLayer whose style is only a LabelStyle. That is what Mapbox GL does with its symbol layers. HowTo Label your data shows how the attributes get there.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Each data layer has its own Enabled. Switch one off: the other is untouched, and the one you hid keeps its features and its style, so switching it back on costs nothing. That is Mapsui's own visibility flag being set rather than the layer being taken apart - Layers Built does not move, and a disabled layer draws nothing at all, checked in the renderer itself.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;The basemap is the general XYZ node, and the template is OpenStreetMap's own written out. Point it at any other provider and nothing downstream changes - but check that provider's terms, and put their required credit in Attribution. A template without {x}, {y} and {z} is refused with a reason rather than used, because every tile would otherwise resolve to the same URL and the map would fill with one image repeated.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Frame the line asks ZoomToLayer to put the view where that layer's data is. It is triggered rather than continuous: framing every frame would pin the view and the map could not be dragged. An empty layer moves nothing, so a bang landing before the data is harmless.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Enabled starts OFF. Opening a document in vvvv runs it, so a map that fetched on open would give you no chance to decline. Switch it on to see the map.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Watch Layers Built: it should settle at 1 and stay. A number climbing frame after frame means something rebuilds the layer every frame, and every rebuild starts a fresh round of tile requests. That once exhausted a machine of ephemeral ports and took a home network down. Close vvvv if you see it climb.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Tiles that were drawn are cached under %LOCALAPPDATA%\VL.Mapsui\tiles, which is what the OpenStreetMap tile policy asks for. A session is a few megabytes. Delete the folder to reset.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;TileCache decides where tiles go, and it is the only thing that does: hand its output to the layer's Cache pin, or leave that pin unconnected for the same default. Leave its Folder pin UNCONNECTED too - do NOT connect an empty Path IOBox, because there is no such thing. VL resolves an empty Path against the document and hands the node this patch's own folder, which wrote 444 tiles into two repositories on 2026-08-14 while every pin still read correctly.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <!--
            The basemap is the general XYZ node rather than the OpenStreetMap one, and the template
            below is OpenStreetMap's own written out - which is the point: swap the URL for any
            other provider and everything downstream is unchanged. CHECK THAT PROVIDER'S TERMS
            FIRST, and put their required credit in Attribution: the Attribution widget draws what
            the layers carry, so a layer with none contributes nothing to it and says nothing about
            it either.
          -->
          <Pad Id="NvXojaTPUJZ35ElHNE2oWj" Comment="URL Template" Bounds="300,180,420,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="LWN0neX44CbQuPiXEXCHhO" Comment="Attribution" Bounds="300,205,420,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="© OpenStreetMap contributors">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="UnaIkq8cPr0a4UZQVn7ji7" Comment="Enabled" Bounds="79,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="false">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="CNYLiTg3BUtmCJlFwHyUjv" Comment="Cache To Disk" Bounds="207,280,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="true">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="79,340,150,19" Id="JqwwJBWIvaSJq4DTAz8vuN">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="XYZ" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="EwCUX43bSdeeUIwMo6nnKl" Name="URL Template" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="JBzzMJAER6z1AtD4067pl2" Name="Attribution" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Usi9xynIVqJWvRhEvGVOYQ" Name="Enabled" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="ARy89W2GJw4s60rzwfmBsV" Name="Cache" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="VE109xy4WqBycyAwxMeCrD" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="MVGJGduk0mPWJznoGv9YVX" Name="Layers Built" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="HwRnfleRlGfpKEI7pXlafv" Name="Cache Status" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="RgIIgaq8NiTBppqeaxZgPe" Comment="Layers Built" Bounds="153,391,80,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <!--
            ***** the zoom levels a layer belongs to *****

            Order decides what covers what. It does not reduce anything - twenty layers all draw,
            whatever the order. VisibleRange is the thing that reduces: outside its range Mapsui
            skips the layer entirely. Measured, it is a hard cut - 91204 pixels inside, 0 outside.

            That is how a real map stays readable. City blocks at country zoom are a grey smear;
            country outlines at street zoom are a line off the edge of the screen. Every GIS says
            which scales a layer belongs to, and this is how you say it here.

            TRY: zoom out past level 10 and the line leaves; zoom back in and it returns. The area
            and the basemap are untouched, because the range is set per layer.

            The two pins run OPPOSITE to the numbers underneath. Mapsui stores this as MinVisible
            and MaxVisible in RESOLUTION - map units per pixel - where a higher zoom level is a
            SMALLER number. So From Zoom sets MaxVisible. The node hides the inversion; Status
            tells you what it understood, and refuses a backwards range rather than making the
            layer vanish at every zoom.
          -->
          <Pad Id="R8SHZCaDY6VHiZWP62P04D" Comment="From Zoom - most zoomed OUT" Bounds="330,455,180,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="10">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="IDKz5tvZ3Q43MTk2oTv3p8" Comment="To Zoom - most zoomed IN" Bounds="330,480,180,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="30">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="GUmRf85HlFysFTbfJmrKji" Comment="Range Status" Bounds="530,505,320,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />
          <Node Bounds="330,505,130,19" Id="RtKJyrFyEoplkwnyNJQdsX">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="VisibleRange" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="DAetmSHmMADzgJy2JFaqHY" Name="Layer" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="S6BrVXJEISDTxzjjT4BEA7" Name="From Zoom" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="I2fzCE29qYHLFYY4SbbCvV" Name="To Zoom" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="UwHpYFwSsePi2oK0vUog20" Name="Status" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="HWuR42AKlsS0QAWUMusfR5" Name="Output" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Node Bounds="87,523,39,19" Id="IuHPlniMpFcdUZg9WNt7Xp">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Cons" />
              <CategoryReference Kind="RecordType" Name="Spread" NeedsToBeDirectParent="true" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="FitnqKKJuItGI6PwD5m2Mp" Name="Input" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Udad8igNKGlXkj4SIfvVV8" Name="Input 2" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Koh07WKP1qOyx3ZRqLWukD" Name="Input 3" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Obo0KlAOX8uJTLEhkSgG4Y" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="QTNlTyezfmbasb8gEcPG61" Comment="Initial Longitude" Bounds="140,583,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="135.7581">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="I8MAlGEJKxag8SUuQTLx71" Comment="Initial Latitude" Bounds="229,544,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="34.9859">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float64" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="MU5GcscWwFrk45xrCPm07u" Comment="Initial Zoom Level" Bounds="329,583,50,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="15">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Integer32" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <!--
            ***** your own shapes, from here down *****

            The shape has to come from somewhere, and that somewhere is NOT VL.Mapsui: this package
            draws geometry, it does not create it. In a real patch the geometry comes from VL.NetTopologySuite,
            from a file, or from a service. Here it is a fixture so the example stands on its own.

            Read WKT is one way in and the shortest one to read on a page. VL.NetTopologySuite also
            builds geometry coordinate by coordinate - Coordinate, LinearRing, Polygon - and its own
            HowTo Create a polygon shows that. Either way what arrives here is the same type, which
            is the point: geometry is a TYPE, not a format.
          -->
          <Pad Id="IrotR4gFylcZ62ydUXjBUC" Comment="WKT - edit me" Bounds="300,430,420,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="POLYGON ((135.7551 34.9834, 135.7611 34.9834, 135.7611 34.9884, 135.7551 34.9884, 135.7551 34.9834))">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>

          <Node Bounds="300,470,90,19" Id="F5vfpYSEn6YZY4v3D0jivA">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="NTS.IO" LastDependency="VL.NetTopologySuite.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Read WKT" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="Kb4sXPGCYJ0jU6Zyvu99Tv" Name="WKT" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="UtvFvoNAEkKql434eX5gs6" Name="Factory" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="E0X52rFVPedYg2yFKnLn8M" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="OgXXHEYRAmZYPBiQSUUGoM" Name="Success" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="RS6Hqm6oVzhIG8hIyXH2eJ" Comment="parsed?" Bounds="420,470,60,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" />

          <Node Bounds="300,510,110,19" Id="LKlHCGkEW27uDksjQ03tsc">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Feature" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="VZkOsrOFuCUESnjJOlfiv8" Name="Geometry" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="T4DyhbpJF7z3MVEDGgU1l4" Name="Attributes" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="T3xaP10ssIBu1W84JenuLS" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>

          <Node Bounds="300,550,39,19" Id="A4jSu2sjauZP2s8LlxSayy">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Cons" />
              <CategoryReference Kind="RecordType" Name="Spread" NeedsToBeDirectParent="true" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="Hv9nORTiBeD0FjRJwQP1zt" Name="Input" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="LVp2NShI38PM2uwngTMRoZ" Name="Input 2" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="PAwh0bTqOnKYu3GBgYxASP" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>

          <!--
            The style is a value of its own, and a node rather than pins on the layer. Leave it
            unconnected and the layer still draws something visible - good defaults are part of the
            public API.
          -->
          <Node Bounds="520,510,130,19" Id="T4PA3iOraHVrJGn6DvQeiR">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Styles" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="VectorStyle" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="NWFqDIKalaxaGQVLqfQHBi" Name="Fill Color" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="F00RpgC9bhD9HuhOAUsoNX" Name="Line Color" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="UumeV5rj8Ly2LZmKZzyjuo" Name="Line Width" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="VMyWIw2DDLYJnnMn4lhUAv" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>

          <Node Bounds="300,590,150,19" Id="RYg4JjkLhluvFy6irExfYD">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Layers" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="FeatureLayer" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="AMeaHKeDjwSfsDqswpSIBi" Name="Features" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Sb8LY47ypOqKRxpyRAwgiA" Name="Style" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="QZFxWGTEIhgXeyTjsnYIa2" Name="Enabled" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="U7vVs30TfyVg6lNRtRKCvd" Name="Name" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="UX2Q4zuDSJ3FicIQjybU4g" Name="Layers Built" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="Ck0b9Fm6W6GxEbNGJgeI05" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="RWntibAW5PnC5Bqh3ydH21" Comment="Area layer" Bounds="480,590,35,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="True">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="ImmutableTypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>

          <!--
            ***** the second data layer *****

            The same five nodes again, with its own WKT and its own style. Two things this is for:
            layer ORDER is spread order, so whichever goes into Cons later lands on top; and each
            layer switches off on its own, without disturbing the other or losing anything.

            Enabled here is Mapsui's visibility flag - the layer keeps its features and its style
            while it is hidden, so switching it back on costs nothing.
          -->
          <Pad Id="SOzPULPhPtLmKyFSGnKNpH" Comment="WKT - the line" Bounds="760,430,420,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="LINESTRING (135.7500 34.9800, 135.7581 34.9859, 135.7700 34.9900, 135.7800 34.9860)">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Node Bounds="760,470,90,19" Id="BZlieK3G3oYyBl2RmTgGJN">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="NTS.IO" LastDependency="VL.NetTopologySuite.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Read WKT" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="Mksa80VrNZODDVf4Zj6d5L" Name="WKT" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="RXkI68Epytf5h8qukPb1nV" Name="Factory" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="EpsXMjR4q4xQXpisobpqZs" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
            <Pin Id="TVxlb6yz3R7SRFkGGREOwF" Name="Success" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Node Bounds="760,510,110,19" Id="Uoh5qzwT2aSLJLn6h5zET1">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Feature" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="GN9SDh2iVoA4yCclKA6DcG" Name="Geometry" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="O4J61zLHXFVKdDS1oWVZOj" Name="Attributes" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="JSd3s0cF90LDhjIzZSrtvv" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Node Bounds="760,550,39,19" Id="RHQRP8G9Rr6nXFPxmAnmyB">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Collections.Spread" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="OperationCallFlag" Name="Cons" />
              <CategoryReference Kind="RecordType" Name="Spread" NeedsToBeDirectParent="true" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="JnUaZirjDd1GMOm5Z0Q3lr" Name="Input" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="RhMeLph5eSqBm53BytyFW6" Name="Input 2" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="I3d9dYXGOSjDDBvAjkfYYW" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Node Bounds="980,510,130,19" Id="SxWccisfXGqlKUSEwzpSnu">
            <p:NodeReference LastCategoryFullName="Mapsui.Styles" LastDependency="VL.Mapsui.vl">
              <Choice Kind="NodeFlag" Name="Node" Fixed="true" />
              <Choice Kind="ProcessAppFlag" Name="VectorStyle" />
            </p:NodeReference>
            <Pin Id="DSyFLBweSyILcm4t1LodUK" Name="Fill Color" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="V6TiwleTonxCnOcltBvwLd" Name="Line Color" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="TvS4o8Nz6fWQ6nbCAYS4Pt" Name="Line Width" Kind="InputPin" />
            <Pin Id="RTSGgT8WWTuIUNlHiQetDG" Name="Result" Kind="OutputPin" />
          </Node>
          <Pad Id="P4fJthVdETw97wyAcCWNc1" Comment="Line Color" Bounds="1130,510,143,20" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="0.1, 0.3, 0.9, 1">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Color" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="RGBA" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="TowVxJgT4jETPhzJ06GznB" Comment="Line Width" Bounds="1130,535,62,15" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="6">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Float32" />
